{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015","id":939517,"title":"Werewolf 2015","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-29T07:30:15-07:00","id":939517,"title":"Werewolf 2015","content":"I am trying to construct a Werewolf 2015 conversion (I have done a similar conversion already for Vampire) and I was wondering if anyone is willing to share their changes to Werewolf canon that would allow such a conversion. I have determined that several propositions must be true: a) the Apocalypse could not have happened (obviously), b) that the Red Star could not appear in the sky (otherwise the first proposition would not be true), c) that new Garou (and Fera) would have to have undergone the Change since 2000 (otherwise the first and second propositions really do not matter), and d) that the world appears to be identical to our world (otherwise it would not be a dark reflection of our world, a world of darkness, but a twisted shadow of our world).<br /> <br /> One of the changes that I am making is that the Gurahl discovered DNA in 2000. After two years of debating, they forcefully took over the facility in 2002 because they could not ignore the potential of using genetic engineering to spread the genetic signatures of the Changing Breeds through the human and animal population. After their takeover, they gave anyone who was responsible for atrocities against the Garou to their associates in the Garou Nation, which gained them some grudging respect from the Garou. They have used the technology that they gained from the takeover from DNA to discover the surviving kinfolk of the Camazotz Fera in 2004 and, in 2006, started to import them from Mexico and Central America. In 2008, they succeeded, with the help of the Uktenu and the Wendigo, in freeing Turtle from its Weaver prison, in exchange for promising to help resurrect the Croatan Tribe from the Croatan Kinfolk among the Uktenu and the Wendigo Kinfolk). In 2010, they started, with the help of Turtle, to aid the first Camazotz in nearly five hundred year to experience the Change. In addition, they have started to spread the Gurahl genetic signature through the North American Black Bear population (the North American Black Bear has a wild population of around a million, meaning that the Gurahl have a potential population of animal Kinfolk that is five times that of the global population of wolves in the wild).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T18:18:16-07:00","id":939884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015#post939517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am trying to construct a Werewolf 2015 conversion (I have done a similar conversion already for Vampire) and I was wondering if anyone is willing to share their changes to Werewolf canon that would allow such a conversion. I have determined that several propositions must be true: a) the Apocalypse could not have happened (obviously), b) that the Red Star could not appear in the sky (otherwise the first proposition would not be true), c) that new Garou (and Fera) would have to have undergone the Change since 2000 (otherwise the first and second propositions really do not matter), and d) that the world appears to be identical to our world (otherwise it would not be a dark reflection of our world, a world of darkness, but a twisted shadow of our world).<br /> <br /> One of the changes that I am making is that the Gurahl discovered DNA in 2000. After two years of debating, they forcefully took over the facility in 2002 because they could not ignore the potential of using genetic engineering to spread the genetic signatures of the Changing Breeds through the human and animal population. After their takeover, they gave anyone who was responsible for atrocities against the Garou to their associates in the Garou Nation, which gained them some grudging respect from the Garou. They have used the technology that they gained from the takeover from DNA to discover the surviving kinfolk of the Camazotz Fera in 2004 and, in 2006, started to import them from Mexico and Central America. In 2008, they succeeded, with the help of the Uktenu and the Wendigo, in freeing Turtle from its Weaver prison, in exchange for promising to help resurrect the Croatan Tribe from the Croatan Kinfolk among the Uktenu and the Wendigo Kinfolk). In 2010, they started, with the help of Turtle, to aid the first Camazotz in nearly five hundred year to experience the Change. In addition, they have started to spread the Gurahl genetic signature through the North American Black Bear population (the North American Black Bear has a wild population of around a million, meaning that the Gurahl have a potential population of animal Kinfolk that is five times that of the global population of wolves in the wild).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no guarantee that you could use DNA (the hereditary macromolecule polymer) to identify Garou kin from Fera kin. Also, Gurahl don't have the numbers to take over all of the facilities of DNA (the organization), when they share so many of the same vulnerabilities as Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T19:18:09-07:00","id":939905,"title":"","content":"Actually, DNA has been successful in using biological and genetic markers to find Kinfolk (Book of the Weaver, p. 97), as they have been able to find unaware Kinfolk. The advantage that the Gurahl have over the Garou is that DNA is unaware of their existence and their capabilities. The Gurahl are also very, very careful.<br /> <br /> The Gurahl do not need to do a frontal assault in Crinos form, they just have to strategic, something that the Garou would lack under the same circumstances. There are 200 Gurahl, not counting Sleepers, and a group of five could cripple DNA by using their stepping ritual to steal into the homes of their lead researchers and their top executives, since they are not in the habit of using reflective surfaces to travel. They would drop from the Umbra to the Earth(which is an instant process for Gurahl because of their connection to the Earth) to capture and extract their targets from their homes in the middle of the night. Executives and researchers can be given to the Garou for justice in exchange for assistance in disrupting DNA. After a few months, the Gurahl could use financial resources gained from accessing the bank accounts of the extracted executives to engage in a forceful financial takeover of DNA. Just a thought...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T19:31:44-07:00","id":939907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015?p=939905#post939905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, DNA has been successful in using biological and genetic markers to find Kinfolk (Book of the Weaver, p. 97), as they have been able to find unaware Kinfolk. The advantage that the Gurahl have over the Garou is that DNA is unaware of their existence and their capabilities. The Gurahl are also very, very careful.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, what I'm saying is that the markers might be the same between Garou and Fera. So there would be no distinguishing between Camazotz kin and Garou kin, possibly. DNA doesn't make the changer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Gurahl do not need to do a frontal assault in Crinos form, they just have to strategic, something that the Garou would lack under the same circumstances. There are 200 Gurahl, not counting Sleepers, and a group of five could cripple DNA by using their stepping ritual to steal into the homes of their lead researchers and their top executives, since they are not in the habit of using reflective surfaces to travel. They would drop from the Umbra to the Earth(which is an instant process for Gurahl because of their connection to the Earth) to capture and extract their targets from their homes in the middle of the night. Executives and researchers can be given to the Garou for justice in exchange for assistance in disrupting DNA. After a few months, the Gurahl could use financial resources gained from accessing the bank accounts of the extracted executives to engage in a forceful financial takeover of DNA. Just a thought... </div> </div> </div>Cooperation with the Garou is a breakdown point. The bigger one is that they, as a whole, are less familiar with modern technology than most Garou are. Also, those 200 are usually off doing their actual duties to Gaia, which doesn't leave much time to engage in an umbral raid in sync with a number of other Gurahl, each in one of DNA's many offices owlrdwide, some of which might be in hostile territory where the Gurahl would be fools to enter the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Edit: Seriously, why the Gurahl and not the Bastet and Corax? Leave the Gurahl at your rendezvous point and have them play good cop to a Bastet's bad cop in sorting out captives. Do not have them go and try to sneak into the facility themselves, alone, it won't end well. Also, Corax will be unaffected by the silver and bear mace that are going to get tossed around, and no one is likely to guess that they should use gold instead, let alone budget for it while also buying silver rounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 07-30-2016, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T10:23:07-07:00","id":940133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015?p=939905#post939905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Gurahl do not need to do a frontal assault in Crinos form, they just have to strategic, something that the Garou would lack under the same circumstances. There are 200 Gurahl, not counting Sleepers, and a group of five could cripple DNA by using their stepping ritual to steal into the homes of their lead researchers and their top executives, since they are not in the habit of using reflective surfaces to travel. They would drop from the Umbra to the Earth(which is an instant process for Gurahl because of their connection to the Earth) to capture and extract their targets from their homes in the middle of the night. Executives and researchers can be given to the Garou for justice in exchange for assistance in disrupting DNA. After a few months, the Gurahl could use financial resources gained from accessing the bank accounts of the extracted executives to engage in a forceful financial takeover of DNA. Just a thought...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also adding on that while Gurahl can instantly step into the material, so can any shapechanger (that can sidestep in the first place) with 3 successes on their gnosis role. There doesn't seem to be any reason at all not to have the Garou just do what you want the Gurahl to do. I don't understand the idea that the Gurahl would somehow be better than the Garou and organized tactical strategy. That concept is bizarre to me.<br /> If they dropped everything else they needed to do (something you want the Gurahl to do) just a portion of the Glasswalker tribe could do all of this no problem if they really needed to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T11:46:45-07:00","id":940168,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that the Gurahl would be more interested in the applications of genetic engineering and biotechnology than the Glass Walkers. While Glass Walkers are aligning with the Weaver, they are more interested in hard tech than soft tech. Anyway, I think that the Garou are temperamentally more likely to do a frontal assault against the labs than to strategically attack the executives and researchers at their homes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T13:08:20-07:00","id":940205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015?p=940168#post940168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think that the Gurahl would be more interested in the applications of genetic engineering and biotechnology than the Glass Walkers. While Glass Walkers are aligning with the Weaver, they are more interested in hard tech than soft tech.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think that the Garou are temperamentally more likely to do a frontal assault against the labs than to strategically attack the executives and researchers at their homes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find I disagree with pretty much the entirety of this post.<br /> <br /> Saying that Garou (Glasswalkers in particular) aren't interested in &quot;soft tech&quot; I would argue is only your opinion. There is a metis Child of Gaia specifically trying to revive the Bunyip (with abysmal results) through genetic engineering. Glasswalers are supposed to be trying to remain on the cusp of technology. That doesn't just refer to hardware. Also, Glasswalkers are somewhat known for &quot;monkeywrenching&quot; which is exactly the infiltration and espionage you think the Garou are unfit for.<br /> I would wager my mental picture of Garou warfare is different than yours. Frontal assaults are reserved for when they would work. Garou are more than capable of coming up with strategies that aren't &quot;Garou smash!&quot;. <br /> <br /> Next...there are a great many things the Gurahl assisting the Garou would accomplish. The Garou would not (and don't have to) rely on the Gurahl to fight their fights for them. Everything you would have the Gurahl do in this scenario, the Garou can do better. It's just a matter of organization, which I would also argue the Garou are better at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T16:02:33-07:00","id":940316,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your interest in the DNA arc, but I was really wondering what elements you would add to reflect the changes from 1999-2015 that would be part of a Werewolf 2015?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T16:15:52-07:00","id":940320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015?p=940205#post940205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find I disagree with pretty much the entirety of this post.<br /> <br /> Saying that Garou (Glasswalkers in particular) aren't interested in &quot;soft tech&quot; I would argue is only your opinion. There is a metis Child of Gaia specifically trying to revive the Bunyip (with abysmal results) through genetic engineering. Glasswalers are supposed to be trying to remain on the cusp of technology. That doesn't just refer to hardware. Also, Glasswalkers are somewhat known for &quot;monkeywrenching&quot; which is exactly the infiltration and espionage you think the Garou are unfit for.<br /> I would wager my mental picture of Garou warfare is different than yours. Frontal assaults are reserved for when they would work. Garou are more than capable of coming up with strategies that aren't &quot;Garou smash!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Next...there are a great many things the Gurahl assisting the Garou would accomplish. The Garou would not (and don't have to) rely on the Gurahl to fight their fights for them. Everything you would have the Gurahl do in this scenario, the Garou can do better. It's just a matter of organization, which I would also argue the Garou are better at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glass Walkers are an exception to Garou not generally having powers that can be bent to subtle measures. Control Simple or Complex Machine, Cybersenses, Signal Rider, and Doppleganger are all incredible advantages. Whether this is a lucky accident or not, this also means that they most fit the horror movie saws of an unstoppable monster who can show up anywhere without warning and take away all of your precious advantages of technology, leaving you, as a human dependent upon those things, utterly helpless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T19:54:54-07:00","id":940402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015?p=940316#post940316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for your interest in the DNA arc, but I was really wondering what elements you would add to reflect the changes from 1999-2015 that would be part of a Werewolf 2015?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for participating in the tangent then.<br /> <br /> On your story, I think you give far too much credit for the Gurahl accomplishing all of those things. Is this storyline exclusively for playing a Gurahl game? It does make the Garou out to be pretty incompetent, since the Gurahl discover DNA and within 2 years they do what the Garou haven't managed in at least a decade. It's more far fetched since the Gurahl suffer pretty much all of the same weaknesses as Garou, so there is no reason DNA would be any more vulnerable to Gurahl attack then to Garou.<br /> Next the Gurahl somehow bring back Turtle? To me, that kind of comes out of nowhere. Turtle should most likely be bound somewhere in the Umbra, away from the Material which is where the Gurahl are at their most powerful thematically.<br /> There are at least 2 story points that hinge on discovering Kinfolk and having them breed true. I personally feel like this would be a much better arc for returning or resurrected Apis. You seemed to have rolled their aptitudes into the Gurahl. Maybe the Gurahl could somehow bring them back, and they (the Apis) could manage all of this Kinfolk breeding stuff and resurrect lost breeds from their descendant kinfolk.<br /> I suppose I'm just not sure how or why the Gurahl manage to do all of this, especially in so few years.<br /> I doubt you are interested in alternative ideas, but I think having a coalition of North American shapeshifters would have a much better chance of making sweeping events like this happen, and would be much more inclusive in the story. There are just too many other shapeshifters that would be much much better than the Gurahl at these tasks (which includes the Garou).<br /> Also...why are the Gurahl not already coming from the black bear population? Black bears make up a significant portion of the Forest Walkers.<br /> <br /> So yea, me personally, during the 15 years, I would have the North American shifters follow example/success of the Ahadi and form their own coalition. You could have the center of said coalition be the Gurahl and the Wendigo and Uktena if that's the way you want to go. That would also be an interesting shift in power from the European Garou tribes dominating to the native shifters descendants having more influence. Accomplishing the story points you have above would go a long way towards showing said coalition's solidarity and strength. Just a few thoughts off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Again, apologies for not responding more directly to the OP.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T20:16:34-07:00","id":940411,"title":"","content":"It is fine. Thank you for the suggestions. The Fera in the North and South America are primarily Native American, though the Garou and Ratkin seem to be primarily European. An American version of the Ahadi) would be a powerful force against the Wyrm, though I am not quite sure if the European Garou would be willing to join. Perhaps by 2015, the Native American Fera and Garou have unified into an American Alliance, but the European Garou are refusing to join? <br /> <br /> It would make for an interesting series of campaigns to have the Native American Alliance and the European Garou trying to compete for the most destruction of the forces of the Wyrm. Would the European Garou be willing to apologize for their arrogance, or would their pride be too great to recognize that their actions were motivated by prejudice? On the other side, could the American Alliance start to increase their numbers? The Gurahl needs more than 200 members, the Nuwisha need more than 100 members, etc. If they cannot find or create more Kinfolk, then the American Alliance would not last for long...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T20:40:30-07:00","id":940420,"title":"","content":"Ok, let's remember that the America's are far more diverse then just Native American and European, and that includes the fera. The Mokole for example have a heavy dose of African ancestry for example, along with Garou tribes like the CoG's, Gnawers, Furies, Glass Walkers....tribes tied more to ideas then human cultures not being purely European in ancestry, along with ratkin being far from picky, and a lot of other fera don't seem to be all that exclusive to what humans they breed with (Nuwisha book states all humans are acceptable for kin, Corax never really state &quot;only white people and Native Americans&quot;, and with how much Native peoples did intermarry with African Americans to say you can't have an African American in any of the fera groups for example is also kinda short sighted, or the fact that Asians have been in this side of the world for quite the while as well....) and this post I typed while admittedly only thinking of the United States and not Latin America or the Caribbean...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T21:09:57-07:00","id":940438,"title":"","content":"<br /> First, agreeing with all of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1179_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1179\" data-vbnamecard=\"1179\">CeltSPZ</a>'s points.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015?p=940411#post940411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It is fine. Thank you for the suggestions. The Fera in the North and South America are primarily Native American, though the Garou and Ratkin seem to be primarily European. An American version of the Ahadi) would be a powerful force against the Wyrm, though I am not quite sure if the European Garou would be willing to join.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I was thinking of the Fera (Garou included) who are traditionally native. Not necessarily the human counterparts. So Wendigo and Uktena, Gurahl, Qualmi and Pumunca and Nuwisha and Corax would be a great starting point. I'm starting with thinking of only the top 2/3 of North America here. You have a few Mokole, but maybe not enough to make a real presence. You can expand the idea to include Central America and then to South America, but I think getting that far in just 15 years is asking <u>a lot</u>. Besides, having that expansion/recruitment happen over the course of a game would be a lot of fun.<br /> I don't count the Ratkin for a few reasons. They're kind of crazy. They're paranoid. The native Ratkin will have been killed off and taken over by the invading European Rats. Think what happened for Garou but arguably worse. This also assumes you even put Ratkin on the continent prior to the Europeans. I certainly do, but in canon it is very questionable. <br /> Rokea don't care and aren't going to join. Ananasi also won't. Nagah are obviously out. Ajaba and Kitsune don't exist in any significant numbers for this. I mentioned Mokole already (in my mind, they don't factor in unless you start in South America and work your way up, but that cuts out the Wendigo mostly and I think the Qualmi as well). Starting in Central or South America opens up the Balam as possibilities.<br /> It really depends on where you want to start something like this. I personally like the idea of this starting in Canada and working south but that might certainly be just me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015?p=940411#post940411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Perhaps by 2015, the Native American Fera and Garou have unified into an American Alliance, but the European Garou are refusing to join?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, this is how I envisioned it. The European-descended Garou have burned so so many bridges. The bulk of them may very well may not be invited to join. I could see some Garou from the other tribes joining as individuals, but I would keep their numbers deliberately low. Children of Gaia mostly, but some others. But for Wendigo and Uktena it would be the majority of the tribe which would put those tribes as being the primary Garou membership in this coalition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015?p=940411#post940411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It would make for an interesting series of campaigns to have the Native American Alliance and the European Garou trying to compete for the most destruction of the forces of the Wyrm. Would the European Garou be willing to apologize for their arrogance, or would their pride be too great to recognize that their actions were motivated by prejudice? On the other side, could the American Alliance start to increase their numbers? The Gurahl needs more than 200 members, the Nuwisha need more than 100 members, etc. If they cannot find or create more Kinfolk, then the American Alliance would not last for long...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Nuwisha numbers are deliberately low. If for some reason, they needed more, more would come back, but that really shouldn't happen. Gurahl could certainly use more, but that is part of the tragedy that is their lot. I think it is more worthwhile story-wise for them to be a small but powerful part of a bigger whole. They should certainly work on increasing their numbers, but even if they doubled, they would still be a small part of a larger organization. It suits them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T21:44:11-07:00","id":940455,"title":"","content":"Well, they are intended as healers, though I think that they could expand their role to biologists and genetics fairly easily. We also should remember their Kinfolk as well, as they are a real force multiplier for non-combat roles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T21:32:34-07:00","id":941024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015?p=940455#post940455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, they are intended as healers, though I think that they could expand their role to biologists and genetics fairly easily. We also should remember their Kinfolk as well, as they are a real force multiplier for non-combat roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gurahl have fewer kin than anyone else. Also, their role as magical healers isn't necessarily going to overlap with modern disciplines of medicine, since Mother's Touch uses Empathy as of W20, and Rituals can take care of an awful lot of the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T02:40:48-07:00","id":941111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015?p=939884#post939884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no guarantee that you could use DNA (the hereditary macromolecule polymer) to identify Garou kin from Fera kin. Also, Gurahl don't have the numbers to take over all of the facilities of DNA (the organization), when they share so many of the same vulnerabilities as Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>But shouldn't there be a possibility, depending on the mating preferences of the Frea in question?<br /> <br /> I mean today scientists can attribute certain DNA-sequences to certain areas of the world where they are most common. For certain garou tribes their mating partners are historically limited to kin from a certain ethnicity and therefore their respective family lines all share certain DNA-sequences. If identified, one could test any given human's DNA for these sequences and if found, the probability of being true born or kin would be higher than normal. Obviously, that would only work if scientists had a couple of samples from several specific individuals that are definitively garou/kin, from which you could isolate that common sequence. And it would work best only on those tribes who historically limited their mating partners so certain ethnicities. Bone Gnawer or Children of Gaia never did, and Uktena stopped some centuries ago.<br /> <br /> But one could argue, that if one has enough DNA material from, for example, Get of Fenris, one could test how far removed from that any given human is, and therefore how probable it is that he/she is kin or even born true.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: To all those Fera that reproduce in a way similar to the Garou and who historically were limiting themselves mainly to a specific ethnicity as mating partners, the system would work just as well, if one had a large enough set of DNA samples that are guaranteed to be from that breed to start the analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T03:09:24-07:00","id":941120,"title":"","content":"As for the original topic:<br /> <br /> We have played out LARP from 2000 to today and there were no needs to change anything in the setting. We just never started any of the 'Apocalypse' scenarios and never had the 'the last to fight in the Apocalypse is born' reveal. Obviously, everything that happens in real live also happens in our games (so far), so our game has Smartphones and High Speed Internet and surveillance satellites and what not. No biggy. So, I never get why people stated, that there was a need to bring Vampire or Werewolf to 2015. I found al the material was perfectly valid in todays world, just like at the end of revised's run in 2004.<br /> <br /> All the changes that seem to be coming with BNS's Werewolf and whatever Martin has in store for us, I feel they are thrown upon us and not helping or improving the game as it is, but changing it become something else. Doesn't mean something bad, but just not what I want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T08:01:47-07:00","id":941193,"title":"","content":"Well, there would be changes in the supernatural world to reflect the events of the 'real' world. For example, the attack on 9/11 could be a power play by the Assamite clan against the Camarilla and the entire War of Terror could be seen as a conflict between the Assamite and the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T08:02:25-07:00","id":941194,"title":"","content":"Or that the BP Gulf spill was caused by Pentex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T08:58:14-07:00","id":941217,"title":"","content":"I think it was the Strider book that covered 9/11 and they said it was simply humans, which is what I'd prefer honestly. Every major thing in the world really doesn't need to be just another bump (though in this case a big bump) in the night, as for BP that was covered in W20 Rage Across the World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T12:31:11-07:00","id":941341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015?p=941111#post941111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But shouldn't there be a possibility, depending on the mating preferences of the Frea in question?<br /> <br /> I mean today scientists can attribute certain DNA-sequences to certain areas of the world where they are most common. For certain garou tribes their mating partners are historically limited to kin from a certain ethnicity and therefore their respective family lines all share certain DNA-sequences. If identified, one could test any given human's DNA for these sequences and if found, the probability of being true born or kin would be higher than normal. Obviously, that would only work if scientists had a couple of samples from several specific individuals that are definitively garou/kin, from which you could isolate that common sequence. And it would work best only on those tribes who historically limited their mating partners so certain ethnicities. Bone Gnawer or Children of Gaia never did, and Uktena stopped some centuries ago.<br /> <br /> But one could argue, that if one has enough DNA material from, for example, Get of Fenris, one could test how far removed from that any given human is, and therefore how probable it is that he/she is kin or even born true.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: To all those Fera that reproduce in a way similar to the Garou and who historically were limiting themselves mainly to a specific ethnicity as mating partners, the system would work just as well, if one had a large enough set of DNA samples that are guaranteed to be from that breed to start the analysis.</div> </div> </div> </div>DNA isn't spirit stuff. Spirit stuff is one of the key things that makes the staff from a similarly-named company bang its head against the wall, night and day, never sure what piece of the puzzle they're missing. Also, back in Revised, they were completely ignorant of the Fera.<br /> <br /> As for ethnic markers, those are still broad nets, and a lot of Garou wouldn't actually cleave to the ones noted in 1e. Fenrir, for example, were presented as being much more inclusive from an earlier point than in prior editions. Also, the distance of descent you're measuring isn't an origin of something born entirely of flesh, so you can't really expect much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T13:47:22-07:00","id":941385,"title":"","content":"I do not know, I sort of like the Shadowrun 4e take on genetics, that DNA possesses a magical component that may be activated under certain circumstances. Kinfolk would possess such a genetic marker but, since they were not chosen by Gaia to be Garou (or Fera) the magical component would not have been activated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T14:04:19-07:00","id":941393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015?p=941385#post941385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not know, I sort of like the Shadowrun 4e take on genetics, that DNA possesses a magical component that may be activated under certain circumstances. Kinfolk would possess such a genetic marker but, since they were not chosen by Gaia to be Garou (or Fera) the magical component would not have been activated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadowrun is not the WoD. Unless you're playing Mage, in which case... whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T14:12:20-07:00","id":941399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/939517-werewolf-2015?p=941393#post941393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you're playing Mage, in which case... whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually laughed out loud reading this.<br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T04:17:31-07:00","id":941821,"title